 "recommendation": {
  "production_max_rounds": 120,
  "rationale": [
   "2.7x the observed maximum natural convergence round of 44.",
   "mean 23.86 + 11.3 standard deviations.",
   "Raising the ceiling costs ZERO for candidates that converge earlier: exp4_certify.py breaks out of the round loop the moment a full round finds no improving move. The ceiling only costs time for candidates that would otherwise be truncated, which are exactly the ones that should be allowed to finish. Erring high is therefore close to free.",
   "A candidate that actually ran the full 120 would take about 59 minutes (366 + 26.7*120 = 3564s), which is tolerable as a worst case.",
   "It remains low enough that a candidate reaching it is a genuine alarm worth stopping for, rather than a silent multi-hour burn."
  ],
  "alternatives_considered": {
   "100": "2.3x observed max; defensible, slightly less headroom for the 179 unsampled.",
   "200": "known safe -- 0/21 reached it -- but a capped candidate would cost ~95 min, and the extra headroom buys little over 120.",
   "60": "only 1.4x observed max. Too close to the tail given that 21 candidates understate the max of 200. Not recommended."
  },
